    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5092f70ab98082408d19618ec0705dc65a0aaa66132d56fbfbf89389e0c00ebe",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source narrows the counterexample domain in successive, interacting stages: class theorems first remove large structural regions, least-counterexample descent forces the largest remaining prime below log n, a 5-free Euler-product feedback loop lowers that prime bound to 73, and exponent-pattern canonicalization converts the residual case to finite Hardy–Ramanujan checks.",
