    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8780b7763f19c13263904f97090ddbe0884f8899bfaf298a516ef565e0bd1a7f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The strict fixed-t extremal gap e^gamma/zeta(t) turns the t-free classes into bounded-exponent layers below the unrestricted Robin constant; combining that gap with Robin's infinite-counterexample consequence under RH failure forces any such counterexample sequence to leave every fixed layer, so its maximum prime exponent tends to infinity.",
